# Project QA Conventions (retech-web-automation)

## Stack

- Selenium WebDriver + Java + Maven
- TestNG (not JUnit) with suite XMLs at repo root (`testng*.xml`)
- Allure reporting
- Page Objects under `src/test/java/com/retech/web/pageObject`
- Tests under `src/test/java/com/retech/web/tests` (and Cucumber steps under `stepDefination` when applicable)
- Core/driver utilities under `src/test/java/com/retech/web/core` and `utils`

## When generating or changing tests

1. Prefer existing Page Objects / helpers over new parallel abstractions.
2. Follow locator priority from `selenium-java` rules; avoid absolute XPath and `Thread.sleep()`.
3. Keep credentials and environment config in `src/test/resources/config` / env vars — never hardcode secrets.
4. Attach meaningful Allure steps for new flows.
5. If a skill defaults to JUnit 5 / AssertJ / Playwright, adapt to TestNG + this repo's patterns.

## Useful skills (prefer these for this stack)

- Cucumber / Gherkin / steps → `cucumber-skill` + `cucumber-best-practices`
- TestNG suites / groups / parallel → `testng-skill`
- Selenium WebDriver Java → `selenium-skill` or `webapp-selenium-testing`
- REST Assured / API → `api-testing`
- Allure reporting → `allure-configure-reporting`
- Flaky triage → `flaky-test-detective` (pair with project self-heal code under `com.retech.web.selfheal` / `ai`)
- A11y (Selenium) → `accessibility-selenium-testing` or `accessibility-skill`
- CI pipelines → `cicd-pipeline-skill` + project `cicd-testing` rule
- Simplify / cut over-engineering → `ponytail` / `ponytail-review` / `ponytail-audit`

## Useful agent personas

- Selenium work → `.cursor/agents/selenium-test-specialist.agent.md`
- Flaky / failing UI → same specialist + `flaky-test-detective` + `webapp-selenium-testing` / `selenium-skill`
- Refactors / DRY / POM extraction → `.cursor/agents/test-refactor-specialist.agent.md`
- Routing multi-step QA work → `.cursor/agents/qa-orchestrator.agent.md`
- API-only work → `.cursor/agents/api-tester-specialist.agent.md` + `api-testing` skill
